Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:12.706Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:12.706Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f74c677dc36a8922403"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f74c677dc36a8922401", "title": "Chemistry Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f74c677dc36a89223b8", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60da9b4f62f042332c53833a"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87e3"], "question": {"text": "The total number of 'sigma' and 'Pi' bonds in 2-oxohex-4-ynoic acid is ______"}, "options": [{"id": "82dd65", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f74c677dc36a89223b9"}, {"id": "9db5a8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f74c677dc36a89223ba"}, {"id": "d0ac86", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f74c677dc36a89223bb"}, {"id": "22f196", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f74c677dc36a89223bc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f74c677dc36a89223bd", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e567fc499d1e49588fa045"], "concepts": ["60e567fb499d1e49588fa02c"], "question": {"text": "The separation of two coloured substances was done by paper chromatography. The distances travelled by solvent front, substance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;and substance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> from the base line are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>08</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. respectively. The ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math> values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is (Answer the nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "566703", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f74c677dc36a89223be"}, {"id": "4316fa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f74c677dc36a89223bf"}, {"id": "f1dc3f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f74c677dc36a89223c0"}, {"id": "128e3e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f74c677dc36a89223c1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f74c677dc36a89223c2", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["617aa9f6ef3fe65ad8e8445b"], "concepts": ["617aa9f6ef3fe65ad8e8441e"], "question": {"text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of an organic compound was analysed by Kjeldahl&#39;s method for the estimation of nitrogen. If the percentage of nitrogen in the compound was found to be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>42</mn><mo>%</mo></math>, then.......&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mL</mi></math> of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> would have been neutralized by the ammonia evolved during the analysis."}, "options": [{"id": "85672f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f74c677dc36a89223c3"}, {"id": "f759c2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f